{
  "abstract": "Let $B=A+I$ for a hypothetical directed strongly regular graph with parameters $(98,20,9,8,3)$. Fix a full class $C$ of eight equal rows, put $U=N^+[x]\\setminus C$, and suppose the induced functional map has exactly three even basins and the U-to-outside block has rank ten. We prove that all three even basins are isolated two-cycles and that the full $U$-column rank is also ten. Each pair therefore consists of genuine full-row and full-column twins. The proof retains the missing rank-one direction between the eleven-dimensional local row space and the full rank twelve. Complete physical moment systems first exclude the 51 nonpaired maps in an 80-map population cover. If the paired columns lifted in rank, their nonzero differences would be a common signed vector. Minimizing an actual row functional produces an integral class function whose outside sum is negative. Exact seven-vertex arithmetic eliminates 27 of the 29 remaining odd maps; the other two force actual row patterns, and all 112 physical column profiles at those rows are excluded by 142 integer certificates. A standalone independent checker regenerates coverage, replays the certificates, and verifies known graph controls in which a column-rank lift really occurs. The conclusion is conditional on the specified local interface and does not settle the existence problem.",
